+def _park_direct_budget_pause_inline(task: Dict[str, Any], events: Any) -> list:
+    """Park a direct turn's exact budget pause BEFORE its registry entry is released (#1196).
+
+    The turn's ``budget_pause`` event carries its own task record (a direct
+    turn was never in RUNNING). Handing that event to the supervisor loop and
+    unregistering the actor races: between the unregister and the park the
+    SAME id is nowhere — not live, not queued — and a restart in that window
+    fences a saved pause. The direct lane runs inside the supervisor process,
+    so it parks the record itself through the ONE park owner
+    (``events_budget.install_exact_budget_pause``) against the same queue
+    state, under the queue lock, and drops the event from the hand-off. A park
+    that fails leaves the event on the ordinary path (typed, logged), never a
+    silently lost pause. Every other event passes through unchanged.
+    """
